BUSINESS REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (BDR)
1. Business Overview

The project aims to build an on-demand home service platform similar to Urban Company that connects customers with nearby service professionals such as cleaners, electricians, plumbers, and appliance repair technicians.

The platform will allow customers to quickly find reliable workers, get price estimates, book services, track service progress, and pay securely.

Service providers will be able to receive service requests, manage their bookings, and track earnings.

Administrators will manage the platform by approving workers, monitoring bookings, resolving issues, and analyzing system performance.

The system will be developed using the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js).

2. Business Objectives

The main objectives of the system are:

• Provide a fast and reliable platform for booking home services.
• Create job opportunities for local service professionals.
• Allow customers to compare workers based on rating and distance.
• Improve service transparency through tracking and reviews.
• Enable administrators to monitor and manage the entire platform.

3. Business Stakeholders
Stakeholder	Description
Customers	People who need home services
Service Workers	Professionals who provide services
Admin	Platform managers
Business Owners	Owners of the platform
4. Business Requirements
BR1: User Registration

The system must allow customers to create accounts using email or phone.

BR2: Worker Registration

Workers must be able to register and submit verification documents.

BR3: Service Marketplace

Users should be able to browse available services such as cleaning, plumbing, and appliance repair.

BR4: Worker Discovery

Users must be able to find workers based on:

• location
• rating
• service type

BR5: Booking System

Users must be able to schedule services and choose preferred time slots.

BR6: Price Estimation

Users should receive a rough cost estimate before booking.

BR7: Real-time Tracking

Users must be able to track the status of their service request.

BR8: Reviews and Ratings

Users should be able to rate and review workers after completing a service.

BR9: Admin Control

Admin must be able to manage users, workers, services, and bookings.

FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT

Functional requirements describe what the system should do.

1. User Functional Requirements
User Account Management

Users must be able to:

• Register
• Login
• Logout
• Update profile
• Reset password

Service Search

Users must be able to:

• View available services
• Search services
• Filter by price
• Filter by rating
• Filter by distance

Worker Selection

Users must be able to:

• view worker profiles
• see worker ratings
• see worker experience
• choose preferred worker

Service Booking

Users must be able to:

Select service

Select worker

Choose time slot

Confirm booking

Booking Tracking

Users must be able to track booking status:

• Request sent
• Worker accepted
• Worker on the way
• Work started
• Work completed

Service History

Users must be able to view:

• past bookings
• worker details
• price paid
• service date

Payment

Users must be able to pay using:

• UPI
• Card
• Cash

Rating and Feedback

Users must be able to:

• rate worker performance
• write reviews

2. Worker Functional Requirements

Workers must be able to:

• register on the platform
• upload verification documents
• update service availability
• view incoming job requests
• accept or reject bookings
• update job progress
• generate final bill
• view earnings history

3. Admin Functional Requirements

Admin must be able to:

Manage Users

• view users
• block users
• delete users

Manage Workers

• approve worker registrations
• verify documents
• suspend workers

Manage Services

Admin must be able to:

• add new service types
• update service categories
• remove services

Booking Monitoring

Admin must be able to:

• view all bookings
• cancel bookings
• resolve disputes

Analytics Dashboard

Admin must see:

• total users
• total workers
• active bookings
• total revenue

NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

Non-functional requirements define how the system performs.

1. Performance Requirements

The system should:

• support thousands of users simultaneously
• respond within 2 seconds
• handle high traffic during peak hours

2. Security Requirements

The system must ensure:

• encrypted passwords (bcrypt)
• secure authentication (JWT)
• role-based access control
• protection against SQL/NoSQL injection

3. Reliability

The system must ensure:

• data consistency
• automatic error handling
• failure recovery mechanisms

4. Scalability

The system must support:

• horizontal scaling
• cloud deployment
• microservice expansion in the future

5. Availability

The platform should maintain 99.5% uptime.

6. Usability

The application must provide:

• simple user interface
• mobile-friendly design
• easy booking process

7. Maintainability

The system must:

• follow modular architecture
• allow easy updates
• support future feature integration

8. Compatibility

The application must work on:

• Chrome
• Edge
• Firefox
• Mobile browsers

9. Data Integrity

The system must ensure:

• no data duplication
• consistent booking records
• secure storage of personal information

10. Logging and Monitoring

The system should log:

• user activities
• booking operations
• error events

